   "tag": "h1",
   "text": "Healing the Fear of Disappointing Others",
   "section": "comp-m04zcdxw"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Life often asks us to carry a list of expectations, to be kind, be available, be agreeable. And most of us carry these expectations on our shoulders most of our lives without a doubt. And while we strive to meet the world’s demands, we may quietly ignore the deepest call of our own soul.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "But here’s a truth the universe whispers: disappoint everyone else before you disappoint yourself.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "This is not a call to be selfish. It is a call to be aligned. To honour your inner truth, your well-being, and your soul’s path. In hypnotherapy, we see that the real struggle isn’t external, it’s the old, deeply ingrained belief that our worth depends on approval by pleasing others.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Why We Fear Disappointing Others",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "From childhood, our subconscious minds are wired to keep us connected and our spirits learned that approval equals to belong, to be loved. These thoughts can linger within us, creating subtle fear whenever we stand in our truth:",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What if they get upset?",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What will they think of me?",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Will I lose their approval?",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Honouring Yourself is Sacred",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "The aim isn’t to become someone who never disappoints anyone. That’s unavoidable. The aim is to become someone who remains true to themselves confidently, and unapologetically.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "To disappoint others may have a temporary effect, but to disappoint yourself may stay with you through a lifetime. When you stop disappointing yourself, life becomes lighter, freer, and far more authentic.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Those who truly love you do not want the exhausted version of you. They wish for your authentic presence, the radiant, grounded, whole.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "So, Imagine this simple shift. Instead of asking, “What will they think of me?” you ask, “What does my soul need?”",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Hypnotherapy as a Spiritual Practice",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Hypnotherapy is a sacred invitation to reconnect with your inner wisdom. In a state of deep relaxation, your subconscious becomes open to new, empowering beliefs, like releasing the worry of disappointing others, building confidence and boundaries and strengthen your sense of worthiness.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "The purpose is not perfection. The purpose is to live in alignment with your soul freely, confidently, and unapologetically.",
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "If your spirit is ready to awaken and to embrace your deepest truth, hypnotherapy offers a gentle, transformative path forward by guiding you back to the sacred harmony of self, mind, and soul.",
   "section": ""
  },
